SDE WM: SDE's "Wait / Force Close" dialog for windows that do not respond.

0.2.0 Alpha 3.1 (docs/FORCE-CLOSE.md in SDE). Openbox's ping code stays as it
is: closing a window that lists _NET_WM_PING pings it, and a window that has
not answered after two pings (about six seconds) is "Not Responding".

* In place of Openbox's own prompt ("The window ... does not seem to be
  responding. Do you want to force it to exit by sending the terminate
  signal?"), client_prompt_kill() runs "sde-force-close --window XID
  --reason closing": SDE's dialog with the program's icon and name, Wait and
  Force Close (SIGKILL at once, with SDE's checks), which closes by itself
  when the program answers again and asks only once per window. Openbox's
  prompt remains the fallback when sde-force-close cannot be started.
* _SDE_NOT_RESPONDING (CARDINAL) on a client window marks it "Not
  Responding": sde-watchdog sets it for the window the user is using when
  it stops answering, and removes it on the first answer. SDE WM reads it
  on PropertyNotify, so the title gets " - [Not Responding]" and closing
  such a window shows the dialog at once. When SDE WM's own ping finds a
  window dead or alive again, it sets or removes the mark too, so the
  panel and the dialog learn about it.

